  "title": "Funmilayo Ransome-Kuti",
  "summary": "Born on 25 October 1900 in Abeokuta, Nigeria, Funmilayo Ransome-Kuti founded the Abeokuta Ladies' Club in 1944, which became the Abeokuta Women's Union. Her efforts contributed to the abdication of the Alake of Abeokuta in 1948, according to one source. She died on 13 April 1978, the year after a military raid on her son Fela's compound.",
